# Seq annotation: @Seq resolves to Type::Seq(Any) in TypeAssert position and
# in function parameter annotations. [@Seq val] checks that val is a sequence;
# the value passes through unchanged. Seq@String (bare Annotated form) resolves
# to Type::Seq(Str) via resolve_annotated — only valid as a standalone expression,
# not in function parameter position (where the parser accepts bare @Seq only).
[f: [fn [xs@Seq] xs]
 seq_assert: [@Seq [seq 1 [seq 2 []]]]
 param_seq: [f [seq "a" [seq "b" []]]]]
===
Dict({"f": Function(xs), "seq_assert": Seq(Int(1), ...), "param_seq": Seq(String("a"), ...)})
